  He does not say very much. He writes out the receipt with a hand that is not quite as steady as it was, and sands it, and gives it to you, and holds your hand a little longer than is quite the custom. "It will be remembered," he says. "I am not speaking of the loan." You think, going down the stair, that it is exactly the sort of thing that a very careful bank is made to do, and that no one has ever got rich by it.
* Buy a good quantity of the Medici paper at a discount, quietly, through Benedetto, and hold it [once]
