# clerk_cool
{watcher.They} get{watcher.s} up, quickly, when {watcher.they} see{watcher.s} you, and bow{watcher.s}, and do{watcher.es} not quite meet your eye. It is quite a correct, formal bow. There is a small coolness in it, as of a person who has made up {watcher.their} mind not to be hurt.
"The house in Pisa has answered," says {watcher.they}. "It is a very short letter. It says that the pages are to go to Rome, as it was ordered, and that I am to be recalled in the summer." {watcher.They} look{watcher.s} at the water. "I should like to know if that is a thing that you would be sorry about. I do not ask for any reason."
:the_clerk_cool
