# dawn
## The first cock
$ do chart("florence.prisca")
The wind has dropped. The sky over San Miniato has the color of the inside of a white shell, and the lamps at the corners have gone out one by one, with a small sound like a breath being let go.
?if b2.anselm == "asked"
  There is a very old man on a hill who is painting again, and you cannot decide whether to be glad.
?elif b2.anselm == "pressed"
  There is a very old man on a hill who is sitting with his hands over his mouth, and you do not think that you will be able to forget it.
?end
?if b2.medici_paper == "lent"
  In the back office of a house across the way a tired man is sleeping with his head on his arm and a receipt under his hand.
?elif b2.medici_paper == "bought"
  In the strong room of the Banca del Colle there is a bundle of paper in red tape that is worth a good deal more than it cost, and that you do not look at when you pass.
?end
Prisca is at the side door, exactly as she was after the first Thursday, in her cloak, with the thin paper in her hand. It is a good deal thinner than it was. She has been up all night, and she does not show it, except that she has not taken off her gloves.
?if b2.prisca_conspiracy == "told"
  "I have my list," she says. "Eleven names. Four of them are Roman, and two are Florentine, and five are people whom I have never seen." She folds it. "I shall not ask you what you are doing. I think that you will tell me when you can. But I should like to ask you one thing, and I should like an honest answer. When it comes, Signore, whatever it is, I wish to be told before. Not after. It is a thing that I have never asked of anyone."
?else
  "I have my list," she says. "Eleven names. I should like to show it to you, and I think that you know why I do not." She folds it. "I am not asking you for your confidence. I am asking you for one thing, and I should like an honest answer. When it comes, Signore, whatever it is, I wish to be told before. Not after. It is a thing that I have never asked of anyone."
?end
?if b2.paper == "carried"
  She does not mention the box in the cellar. It is a very pointed silence.
?end
:the_promise
* Say that you will tell her, before, whatever it costs ?if b2.prisca_deal != "rival"
  $ b2.prisca_promise = "agreed"
  $ bond.prisca += 3
  $ secrecy -= 1
  $ standing += 1
  "Thank you," says Prisca. It is very quiet. It is the voice of a woman who has been alone in a house for a very long time and has been given a key. She puts out her gloved hand and, for a moment, lays it over yours. "I shall hold you to it," she says. "I do not think that I shall have to."
* Say that you will tell her what you can, when you can, and that she must trust you for the rest
  $ b2.prisca_promise = "hedged"
  $ bond.prisca += 1
  She considers it. It is not a thing that you can read in her face, which is perfectly composed. "That is an honest answer," she says, "and it is not the one that I asked for." She nods, slowly, like a woman accepting a note of hand from a debtor of whom she is fond. "I shall take it."
* Say that there are things that you cannot tell her, even before, and that it is for her own sake
  $ b2.prisca_promise = "refused"
  $ bond.prisca -= 2
  $ secrecy += 1
  There is a pause. Prisca's hand goes to the lace at her throat, and stays there. "For my own sake," she says, evenly. "I have been told that before, Signore, by a number of persons, and each time that I have been told it I have turned out to be the last to hear." She smiles. It is quite a pleasant, level smile. "I shall remember that you said it."
The light comes over the roofs. The first Mass begins, and a bell somewhere in the Oltrarno answers it, a little flat, a little late.
$ do rest()
